<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>A point equidistant from two perpendicular lines</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Give a point \(P\) with whole-number coordinates that is the same distance from the line \(x = {@a@}\) as from the line \(y = {@b@}\), and is not on either line.</p><div>\(P = \big(\)[[input:ans1]], [[input:ans2]]\(\big)\) [[validation:ans1]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The lines \(x = {@a@}\) and \(y = {@b@}\) cross at right angles at \(({@a@}, {@b@})\). The points equidistant from them lie on the two bisectors of the angles between them: the lines through \(({@a@}, {@b@})\) with gradients \(1\) and \(-1\). Start at \(({@a@}, {@b@})\) and move the same number of units across and up (or down), for example \(({@a+2@}, {@b+2@})\), which is \(2\) units from each line, or \(({@a-3@}, {@b+3@})\), which is \(3\) units from each.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: give a point equidistant from two perpendicular lines; any correct point scores. (a, b) is on neither y = x nor y = -x, so the bisectors of the axes are wrong answers. Source: original. */
a: rand_with_prohib(-5,5,[0]);
b: rand_with_prohib(-5,5,[0,a,-a]);
ta1: a+2; ta2: b+2;
/* test points */
t5: first(sublist(makelist(a+b+j,j,1,12), lambda([t], is(t#a) and is(t#b) and is(2*t#a+b))));
g6: first(sublist([2,3,4,5,6], lambda([j], is(abs(a+1)#abs(b+j)))));]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
  <specificfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></specificfeedback>
  <questionnote format="moodle_auto_format">
    <text>a={@a@}, b={@b@}</text>
  </questionnote>
  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Loci: a point equidistant from two perpendicular lines</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.3: Give a point on the angle-bisector locus of two perpendicular grid lines.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is original to this project.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
